        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 232,
      "author": {
        "id": 1348424
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-06-23T08:14:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Multi-upstream interfaces: \nprobably we have to use IpServer#cleanupUpstreamInterface(ifname) to clean the rules from IpServer. Let each IpServer to clear its rules on specific interface or ip family. This may be able to fix the timing problem but that will also increase the rule deletion complexity.\nEx: \n  - is ifname -\u003e ifindex available at that moment? index mapping may have been also removed\n  - current rule deletion function may need to be changed for specific interface and all related testing.\n..\n\nSingle-upstream interface (now):\n  - case b, d rely on IpServer#stopIPv4 to clear rules and downstream information.\n  - case a, c rely on BpfCoordinator#updateUpstreamNetworkState to clear rules only. (keep downstream information because downstream may be still connected)\n\ntest case:\na. Loss upstream interface while tethering\nb. Loss downstream interfaces while tethering\nc. Switch upstream interface while tethering\nd. Enabling NAT failure\n\nIPv4 rule deletion doesn\u0027t rely on IpServer#cleanupUpstream as IPv6 one because case c will call IpServer#cleanupUpstreamInterface only.\n\nEx: \ncase c: rmnet -\u003e wifi\n\nIpServer:\ncase CMD_TETHER_CONNECTION_CHANGED:\n    if (newUpstreamIfaceSet \u003d\u003d null) { // \u003c--- case c doesn\u0027t enter (newSet\u003dwifi)        \n        cleanupUpstream();\n        break;\n    }\n\n    for (String removed : upstreamInterfacesRemoved(newUpstreamIfaceSet)) {\n        cleanupUpstreamInterface(removed);  // \u003c--- case c enters (removed\u003drment)\n    }",
      "parentUuid": "d0c6da8b_514e5bd5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 232,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 232,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "f66792f70625ca4cd9701265f0436351c9af50ce",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
